3. Set private-folder permissions
For each user's private directory:
user1
chmod 700 user1folder

pgaddam2
chmod 700 pgaddam2

user3
chmod 700 user3folder

700 means:
Owner   = RWX
Group   = ---
Other   = ---

Therefore:
/userhome/user1folder
    owner 1000
    RWX    user1 only

/userhome/pgaddam2
    owner 1001
    RWX    pgaddam2 only

/userhome/user3folder
    owner 1002
    RWX    user3 only

This is consistent with Azure's ACL model, where the owning user, owning group, and other permissions are supported for local-user authorization. Named-user ACL entries are not currently supported. 
